                <pb facs="0846" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg758"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consular Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Alexandria</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consular agent, Suez, reports Captain Smith, of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ardova</hi>, informs him letter in Smith’s charge for quartermaster-general
                    United States stores, Manila, taken from him, together with all ship’s papers,
                    by commander of <hi rendition="#italic">Smolensk.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
